# PSD-HTML — Quickstart

Turns a designer's Photoshop email (`.psd`) into a classic-Outlook `.OFT` template, deterministically.

**Start here:** [`docs/TOOL_BRIEFING.md`](docs/TOOL_BRIEFING.md) — what the tool is and who it's for, the workflow, inputs/outputs/clients, how it covers the reported bug list, the QA + security posture, and what's built vs. on the roadmap. The authoring SOP is [`docs/PSD-for-HTML_Authoring-SOP.md`](docs/PSD-for-HTML_Authoring-SOP.md).

## Requirements

- **Python 3.10+** (tested on 3.13).
- **Windows + classic Outlook** (desktop, logged in) — needed only for the `.OFT` conversion,
  link-travel verify, capture, and send-verify. The HTML-emit half runs on any OS.
- Python deps install automatically (below): `psd-tools`, `Pillow`, `numpy`, `resvg-py`.

## Install

```powershell
cd handoff
pip install -e .              # the tool + its runtime deps
pip install -e ".[gui]"       # optional: also the drag-and-drop GUI
```

For a pinned, reproducible environment, install the locked set first:

```powershell
pip install -r requirements.lock
pip install -e . --no-deps
```

## Run — one command (PSD -> .OFT)

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File grammar\Invoke-PsdToOft.ps1 `
    -Psd "path\to\design.psd" `
    -OutDir out\my_email `
    -LinkManifest grammar\links\<name>.links.json `
    -Capture                                          # optional: classic-Outlook screenshot
```

Stages (each gated, non-zero exit on failure): emit Grammar-G HTML -> fidelity gate -> Grammar-G
validation -> convert to `.oft` (Outlook COM, images embedded) -> link-travel verify -> capture.
Output lands in `<OutDir>/`: `bundle/` (HTML), `email.oft` (the shippable template), `capture/`.

## Run — GUI

```powershell
pythonw gui\PsdDropper.pyw       # drag a .psd onto the window; "Edit links..." to set URLs
```

## Run — lower-level CLI

```powershell
psd-html emit  <psd> -o out\bundle --links grammar\links\<name>.links.json   # HTML bundle only
psd-html build <psd> -o tree.json                                            # inspect the IR
psd-html --help                                                              # all subcommands
```

## Verify delivery (optional, sends real mail)

```powershell
# Sends the .oft to an address YOU control and confirms every link survived the wire HTML.
powershell -File grammar\Invoke-OftSendVerify.ps1 -OftPath out\my_email\email.oft `
    -To you@yourdomain.com -LinksReport out\my_email\bundle\links_report.json
```

## Link manifest

Hyperlinks come from a `links.json` next to the PSD (or via the GUI's "Edit links..."). A PSD
carries no link data, so this file is the single source of every URL. See
`grammar/links/announcement.links.json` for the shape (`slots` / `regions` / `inline`).

## Tests (coverage / due-diligence proof)

```powershell
pip install -e ".[test]"
python -m pytest                 # synthetic-fixture suite runs anywhere; real-PSD pins skip
                                 # when the proprietary reference corpus isn't present
```
